light. 

Let me make it clear,
and lend me your ear,
it’s sad to hear
the light in your eyes
is growing dim.

It’s hard to see that light disappear,
but I won’t forget, and I hope it’ll reappear.
So hang in there, hold on tight,
your light will come back to the night.

Take it from me, I’ve walked where you are,
I’m you in a different place, not so far.
Your light will return, I swear,
who knows when, who knows where.

And if you need a friend to ride,
a little pony’s by your side.
Short in stride but steady and true,
it’ll walk the dark road through with you.
